[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2564021354","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100453#issuecomment-2564021354","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100453","id":2564021354,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Y09xq","user":{"login":"JackErb","id":16454787,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDU0Nzg3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16454787?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackErb","html_url":"https://github.com/JackErb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackErb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackErb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackErb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackErb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackErb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackErb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackErb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackErb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackErb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-27T20:46:11Z","updated_at":"2024-12-27T20:46:11Z","body":"Updated docs and now passing tests\r\n\r\nI consider renaming this option to `use_physics_ticks` or `synchronize_to_physics_simulation` but decided to stay with the current name for now. Am certainly open to feedback for what would be a descriptive & discoverable name.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2564021354/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2599694532","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100453#issuecomment-2599694532","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100453","id":2599694532,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6a9DDE","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-18T12:18:00Z","updated_at":"2025-01-18T12:18:00Z","body":"I think this makes sense to do, also because it'll avoid a mismatch between the particle simulation and physics simulation when interpolation is disabled or [not working](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/51318). I'd go as far as saying it should be enabled by default but this would be more invasive. (I doubt it would completely break things in a project still.)","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2599694532/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2599863407","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100453#issuecomment-2599863407","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100453","id":2599863407,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6a9sRv","user":{"login":"timoschwarzer","id":8849554,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4NDk1NTQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8849554?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer","html_url":"https://github.com/timoschwarzer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-18T20:16:18Z","updated_at":"2025-01-18T20:16:18Z","body":"> I consider renaming this option to `use_physics_ticks` or `synchronize_to_physics_simulation`\r\n\r\nCamera*D and AnimationMixer call this `process_callback` with an enum value of either `*_PROCESS_IDLE` and `*_PROCESS_PHYSICS`. It would probably be preferable to align the naming with these.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2599863407/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2696646649","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100453#issuecomment-2696646649","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100453","id":2696646649,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6gu4_5","user":{"login":"ttencate","id":90930,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwOTMw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/90930?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ttencate","html_url":"https://github.com/ttencate","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ttencate/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ttencate/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ttencate/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ttencate/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ttencate/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ttencate/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ttencate/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ttencate/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ttencate/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-04T08:40:11Z","updated_at":"2025-03-04T08:41:00Z","body":"Thanks for the PR! I merged it into `4.4-stable` and tried it out on the MRP from #103244, but unfortunately it doesn't seem to work right — particle positions are still wrong, and enabling `use_physics_step` introduces weird flicker:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6290febb-f843-457c-a1b7-2c8a5134604c\r\n\r\nThis is in the editor, but it happens in the running game too.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nAs for naming, it might make sense to align with [`Camera2D.process_callback`](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_camera2d.html#class-camera2d-property-process-callback) and use the enum from there (suitably moved and aliased for backwards compatibility). (Edit: I noticed @timoschwarzer suggesting the same thing above.)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2696646649/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"ho